-- title:
--   Eisenstein congruences detect m-divisibility in the Hecke algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $m$ be a natural number with $m \ge 2$. Let $f$ be a cusp form of weight $2$ for $\Gamma_0(p)$ all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients (taken with respect to width $1$) lie in the bottom subring of $\mathbb{C}$, and suppose given a sequence $af : \mathbb{N} \to \mathbb{Z}$ whose image in $\mathbb{C}$ realises these coefficients, $af(n) = a_n(f)$ for all $n$. Assume that $af(1)$ is coprime to $m$ in $\mathbb{Z}$, and that for every $n \neq 0$ one has $m \mid af(n) - \sigma'_p(n)\,af(1)$, where $\sigma'_p(n)$ is the sum of those divisors of $n$ not divisible by $p$. Write $\mathbb{T} =$ [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra p 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18), the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(p)))$ generated by the operators $T_\ell$ for primes $\ell \nmid p$ together with $U_q$ for primes $q \mid p$, and let `heckeProj p` be the ring homomorphism from $\mathbb{Z}[X_\ell : \ell \text{ prime}]$ to $\mathbb{T}$ sending $X_\ell$ to $U_\ell$ when $\ell \mid p$ and to $T_\ell$ otherwise. The Eisenstein ideal is the kernel of the evaluation $X_\ell \mapsto 1$ for $\ell \mid p$ and $X_\ell \mapsto 1 + \ell$ otherwise. The conclusion: for every integer $c$, if the image of $c$ under the structure map $\mathbb{Z} \to \mathbb{T}$ lies in the sum of the ideal of $\mathbb{T}$ generated by the image of the Eisenstein ideal and the ideal generated by $m$, then $m \mid c$.
--
--   This is the reduction, in the style of Mazur's study of the Eisenstein ideal on $X_0(p)$, of a lower bound for the index of the Eisenstein ideal to the existence of a single cusp form satisfying an Eisenstein congruence modulo $m$: the functional $t \mapsto a_1(tf) \bmod m$ annihilates the image of the Eisenstein ideal while sending an integer $c$ to $c\,af(1)$. It is used in the computation of the cardinality of the quotient of the weight-two Hecke lattice algebra by the Eisenstein ideal in terms of the Eisenstein numerator.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_eisenstein_injective_of_qCoeff_congr_sigmaPrimeTo.lean

